        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brady%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the late 1800s Brady boasted a weekly newspaper, a bank, grain elevators, and even a pole‑and‑neck yoke factory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofbrady.org/about.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Sacred Heart Catholic Church, constructed in 1910, sits just south of the railroad tracks in Brady.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofbrady.org/about.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Brady was officially laid out in 1889, the same year it was incorporated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brady%2C_Nebraska"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Brady offers small‑town charm, rural Nebraska values, and a surprisingly progressive mindset for a village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofbrady.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Brady sits as Lincoln County's easternmost community, just 2 miles north of Interstate 80 and split by U.S. 30.",
